# Out-of-tree modules (linux-mod-r1) are NOT signed: the image runs
# gentoo-kernel-bin, whose .config names Gentoo's build-host key
# (CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_KEY=/var/tmp/portage/sys-kernel/gentoo-kernel-*/temp/kernel_key.pem),
# which is never shipped -- with USE=modules-sign these die in pkg_setup
# (2026-10-01). The kernel has MODULE_SIG but not MODULE_SIG_FORCE, so it loads
# them unsigned. A user who wants them signed needs their own MOK key, enrolled
# on their machine, and a local rebuild; a binpkg cannot carry that. The global
# SECURITY="modules-sign" (make.conf) stays for whatever can still use it.
net-misc/r8168 -modules-sign
x11-drivers/nvidia-drivers -modules-sign
